NoMercy-only: report the alpha pixel format at stream level

Not an upstream commit -- FFmpeg master behaves the same as stock 8.1.2 here.
Depends on hevc-alpha-videotoolbox.patch; meaningless without it.

With the alpha layer decoding correctly, `ffprobe -show_frames` reports
pix_fmt=yuva420p but `ffprobe -show_streams` still reports yuv420p. The cause
is not probe depth (-probesize/-analyzeduration/-fflags noparse make no
difference): avformat_find_stream_info() resolves the stream parameters from
the extradata and returns "All info found" without ever decoding a slice, so
get_format() -- where the auxiliary alpha layer is picked up and avctx->pix_fmt
becomes yuva420p -- has not run when libavformat copies avctx->pix_fmt into
st->codecpar->format.

This makes export_stream_params(), which runs on the extradata path, apply the
same alpha mapping get_format() would. It cannot call ff_hevc_is_alpha_video()
directly because that reads s->vps, which set_sps() binds later, so the VPS
condition is mirrored against sps->vps instead. map_to_alpha_format() is
defined further down the file and is forward-declared for this.

Only the advertised format changes. get_format() still builds its candidate
list from sps->pix_fmt, so hwaccel negotiation is untouched, and when a
hardware format wins, ff_get_format() overwrites avctx->pix_fmt as before.

Drop this file to fall back to upstream behaviour -- 59-hevc-alpha-layer.sh
applies it only when present.

--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -328,6 +328,10 @@
     return 0;
 }
 
+/* Defined below; forward-declared so export_stream_params() can reach it. */
+static enum AVPixelFormat map_to_alpha_format(HEVCContext *s,
+                                              enum AVPixelFormat pix_fmt);
+
 static void export_stream_params(HEVCContext *s, const HEVCSPS *sps)
 {
     AVCodecContext *avctx = s->avctx;
@@ -336,6 +340,23 @@
     unsigned int num = 0, den = 0;
 
     avctx->pix_fmt             = sps->pix_fmt;
+
+    /* avformat_find_stream_info() resolves stream parameters straight from the
+     * extradata and returns without ever decoding a slice, so get_format() --
+     * where the auxiliary alpha layer is normally picked up -- has not run at
+     * this point. Advertise the alpha pixel format here too, otherwise ffprobe
+     * reports the base-layer format for HEVC-with-alpha video while the frames
+     * it actually decodes are yuva*. Mirrors the condition in
+     * ff_hevc_is_alpha_video(), which cannot be reused here because it reads
+     * s->vps -- only bound later, in set_sps().
+     */
+    if (vps && vps->nb_layers == 2 && vps->layer_id_in_nuh[1] &&
+        (vps->scalability_mask_flag & HEVC_SCALABILITY_AUXILIARY)) {
+        enum AVPixelFormat alpha_fmt = map_to_alpha_format(s, sps->pix_fmt);
+
+        if (alpha_fmt != AV_PIX_FMT_NONE)
+            avctx->pix_fmt = alpha_fmt;
+    }
     avctx->coded_width         = sps->width;
     avctx->coded_height        = sps->height;
     avctx->width               = sps->width  - ow->left_offset - ow->right_offset;
